{
  "id": "serial-recall",
  "term": "serial recall",
  "definition": "Serial recall is remembering a set of items and reproducing them in the same order they were presented. In this context, it refers especially to ordered recall of verbal items in short-term memory, which can be disrupted by irrelevant sounds such as speech, tones, or music.",
